course: dictionary
lesson: 8942
title: Dark shapes and word clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A silhouette is the dark shape or outline of something seen against a brighter background. Clues in the sentence often show you this. In stories, «a silhouette in the doorway» adds mystery, because we cannot see the face.
explain: Look for clue words. In the camera sentence, people with the sun behind them come out as black shapes called silhouettes. The word called tells you that silhouettes are the black shapes. Check by swapping in your meaning: a dark outline makes sense there.
explain: Silhouette can also be a verb. «Silhouetted against» means to appear as a dark shape against a light background. Words that follow a word, like against, give you clues about how it is used.
fact: Silhouette is a French word, spelled S-I-L-H-O-U-E-T-T-E.
fact: It is named after a French government minister, Étienne de Silhouette.
fact: «Silhouette» means the dark shape or outline of someone or something against a brighter background.
fact: In art, a silhouette can be a picture cut out of black paper or painted all black, showing only the outline.
fact: Our eyes adjust to bright and dark at the same time, but cameras struggle, so people with the sun behind them come out as silhouettes.
exercise: In stories, «a silhouette in the doorway» adds mystery. What does silhouette mean here? | A loud bang | *A dark shape against a brighter background | A bright, glowing light | A small wooden door
exercise: Silhouette comes from which language? | German | *French | Latin | Greek
exercise: The tower was ___ against the orange sky. Which word fits? | painted | sparkled | *silhouetted | noisy
test: In art, a silhouette is | *a picture cut out of black paper, showing only the outline | a photograph taken at night | a picture painted in many bright colours
test: Why do cameras struggle with a sunset and a person in front of it? | They are too heavy to carry | They only take pictures in colour | They cannot see the sun | *They cannot adjust to bright and dark at the same time
exam: In science, silhouettes show that | *light cannot pass through solid objects | sound cannot travel through air | shadows are always blue | water is always cold
